      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To solve for \\( y \\) in the equation \\( x^2 + x + 4 = y - 4 \\) given that \\( x = -7 \\), we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Substitute \\( x = -7 \\) into the equation:\n   \\[\n   (-7)^2 + (-7) + 4 = y - 4\n   \\]\n\n2. Calculate each term on the left-hand side:\n   \\[\n   (-7)^2 = 49\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   (-7) = -7\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   4 = 4\n   \\]\n\n3. Add these values together:\n   \\[\n   49 + (-7) + 4 = 49 - 7 + 4\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   49 - 7 = 42\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   42 + 4 = 46\n   \\]\n\n4. The equation now simplifies to:\n   \\[\n   46 = y - 4\n   \\]\n\n5. Solve for \\( y \\) by adding 4 to both sides of the equation:\n   \\[\n   46 + 4 = y\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   y = 50\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\( y \\) is \\(\\boxed{50}\\).",
